      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "AR from a homography: the found poster becomes an ArUco-style marker\n\nexercise_homography_ransac registers two photos; this exercise goes one step further and recovers the poster's 3D POSE from the same homography, exactly as if the poster were one big ArUco marker.\n\n1. The shared 'Feature Match + RANSAC Homography' subgraph matches the poster template (image_a) into the scene photo (image_b) - H maps poster pixels to scene pixels.\n2. 'CV Image Corners' emits the template's four pixel corners (top-left, top-right, bottom-right, bottom-left); cv2.perspectiveTransform projects them through H into the scene - the green outline.\n3. The marker trick: a planar 'CV Points' rectangle gives those corners 3D coordinates on the poster's own plane (width 5 world units, aspect matched, y-up, +z toward the camera - the same per-marker convention 'CV ArUco Board Pose' uses). 'CV Solve PnP (Pose)' with the SOLVEPNP_IPPE planar solver turns the 2D-3D correspondences into rvec/tvec.\n4. 'CV Camera Matrix' supplies the SCENE camera's approximate intrinsics (fx = fy = image width 512, principal point = image centre) - no calibration of the original camera exists, and this is close enough for a convincing composite; swap in 'Calibrate Camera' / 'CV Load Camera Params' when you have the real K.\n5. 'CV Camera Pose To 3D View' (orbit anchor = poster centre) + 'CV Preview 3D (Calibrated Camera)' park the milk truck on the poster in the scene photo, emitting the AR render IMAGE plus silhouette and object-relative depth MASKs. Grab a gizmo (move/rotate/scale) to re-park it and re-run - the placement persists in object_transform.\n\nFailure tolerance: a scene without the poster leaves the subgraph at found=false with an identity homography, so the outline stays at the template position and the pose degrades gracefully - nothing halts. Gate downstream nodes on the subgraph's 'found' output with Basic data handling's if/else if you need a clean passthrough.\n\nThe 3D model must sit in ComfyUI/input/3d/MilkTruck.glb (copy it from example_inputs/, see sources.txt)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
